---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="Ethereal collects nothing. No accounts, no cookies, no analytics. Your inputs stay in your own browser. Here is exactly how that works."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <div class="container-page pt-12 pb-16 sm:pt-16">
    <article class="prose-ethereal max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="text-lg">
        Short version: we do not collect, store or transmit any personal data. There is nothing to
        opt out of.
      </p>
      <h2>What happens to what you type</h2>
      <p>
        Your height, weight, age and other inputs are saved in your browser's{' '}
        <code>localStorage</code> under the key <code>ethereal:profile:v1</code> so that every
        calculator can pre-fill them. That data never leaves your device. You can erase it with the
        Reset button on any calculator or by clearing site data in your browser.
      </p>
      <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p>
        The site sets no cookies and loads no analytics, advertising or social-media scripts. Fonts
        are self-hosted, so no third party sees your visit.
      </p>
      <h2>Hosting logs</h2>
      <p>
        Like every website, the hosting provider that serves these files may keep standard,
        short-lived server logs (IP address, requested page, browser type) for security and capacity
        planning. We do not access or analyse them for anything else.
      </p>
      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy ever changes, the update will be recorded on this page with the date. Last
        updated: 15 September 2026.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
